This is indeed the key questions to be answered by the OP.

I seem to recall that in the OP's post there was mentioned that this
new species should appear late in the game; late to me means Gehennom.
How would these walls appear in mazes? Blocking just one space in a
corridor?

N.B.: It might be an interesting idea to introduce [on a no-teleport
level] a maze full of [non-digable] moving (not fixed) walls; but for
this it would *not* be necessary to make those walls living creatures,
a new maze feature would suffice.[*]

A variant WRT the OP's proposal might be to create living boulders
with some/all properties presented in the original post. In Gehennom,
IME, you often have to push boulders in your way; you cannot easily
circumvent them in a maze corridor (as opposed to the upper levels),
and you often need to look for the stairs under boulders. If contact
with boulders in Gehennom could now be dangerous, that might change
game play a bit in some respect. But, frankly, I don't know.

The original proposal has so many arbitrary looking details, without
answering the primary question.

Janis

[*] There's already a level with moving map features (Plan of Water)
and there's also a patch for moving clouds (for the Plane of Air),
so a new dynamic map with moving maze walls might not be too far off.



